Stream B URB observability had two latent breaks
-------------------------------------------------

Commit 03c7c44 fixes both. Without these the trace looks empty for
the synthetic responder and prints lengths as the literal string "zu".

1. ESP_PLATFORM gate hid all dapprobe trace lines.
   synthetic_device.c gated DAP_TRACE_INFO on `#ifdef ESP_PLATFORM`.
   In this user-c-module + IDF layout, synthetic_device.c gets
   compiled twice: once for the micropython.elf target (without
   -DESP_PLATFORM) and once for __idf_main (with -DESP_PLATFORM).
   The linker keeps the elf-side copy; that copy's DAP_TRACE_INFO
   resolves to `(void)s_urb_verbose;` so dap_cmd_in / dap_resp_out
   never fire even with verbose on. usbip_server.c does not have this
   problem because it gates on MPY_POD_HOST_TEST_BUILD instead.
   Confirmed in the build's compile_commands.json:

     micropython.elf.dir/.../synthetic_device.c.obj : no -DESP_PLATFORM
     __idf_main.dir/.../synthetic_device.c.obj      :    -DESP_PLATFORM

   Fix: switch synthetic_device.c to the same MPY_POD_HOST_TEST_BUILD
   gate as usbip_server.c.

2. %zu format specifier rendered literally as "zu".
   The IDF newlib-nano printf does not implement %zu. Output lines
   like "usbip_complete ... actual=zu" carried no length data. Fix:
   cast through (unsigned) and use %u everywhere on the trace path
   in usbip_server.c, usbhost.c and synthetic_device.c.

The dap_cmd_in / dap_resp_out lines also dump the first 8 bytes hex
so the next pass can match request layout to CMSIS-DAP packet types
without re-instrumenting.

